eed/mint route and the AIF distinction we just recovered.\n\nOne correction to keep the trace honest: after following the older wiring, I did find a new-pattern route—but it is only partially closed. The live pipeline has `library-gap-findings → authoring → authored-seeds → pattern-library`; the later slush spec generalizes that as `policy-hole → candidate-pattern/open → uniform prior`. What is missing is a single formal R17 account and a fully automatic evidence-to-candidate transition. I’m checking a few actual library specimens so R17‴ can be illustrated by real positive and negative cases rather than abstract machinery.\n\nOne correction to keep the trace honest: after following the older wiring, I did find a new-pattern route—but it is only partially closed. The live pipeline has `library-gap-findings → authoring → authored-seeds → pattern-library`; the later slush spec generalizes that as `policy-hole → candidate-pattern/open → uniform prior`. What is missing is a single formal R17 account and a fully automatic evidence-to-candidate transition. I’m checking a few actual library specimens so R17‴ can be illustrated by real positive and negative cases rather than abstract machinery.\n\nI agree: R17‴ is the natural place, and Zaif exposes exactly what it should contain.\n\nOne correction first: after tracing the older material, I did find a partially live authoring route:\n\n`cascade library-gap → authoring → authored seed → pattern library`\n\nThe later slush specification expresses it as:\n\n`policy-hole → candidate-pattern/open → uniform prior → witnessed use`\n\nSo the War Machine can ingest new patterns, but the route is sparse, partly manual, and never became a coherent catalogue pattern. That is what R17‴ should repair.\n\nThe three supplements would then have a clean division:\n\n- R17′ — keep unresolved structural hypotheses explorable. Posterior spread is an honest uncertainty bonus, not EIG.\n- R17″ — generate possible reductions from embedding nearness. “These existing concepts might be mergeable.”\n- R17‴ — generate expansions from evidence-bearing holes. “The existing vocabulary cannot adequately describe this recurring situation.”\n\nA draft pattern would be:\n\n> Pattern Genesis from Evidence-Bearing Holes (R17‴).  \n> If independently recorded episodes, failed retrievals, or policy-holes repeatedly expose a situation that no existing pattern adequately handles; however cascades can only compose existing patterns, embeddings supply similarity rather than justification, and BMR can only compare or reduce represented structure; then bundle the triggering circumstances, memories, rejected near-matches, counterexamples, and a falsifiable predicted outcome into a candidate pattern, admit it to R6 at an explicitly unearned prior, and require repeated witnessed enactment-and-review before promotion. Because structure learning requires expansion of the model’s action vocabulary as well as refinement and reduction of what it already contains.\n\nR18 would audit this claim. R17‴ would probably receive an amber or gray faithfulness classification: it is a principled structure-hypothesis generator, but not itself BMR or a canonical EFE quantity.\n\nWhat Zaif contributes\n\nThe War Machine route begins with relatively coarse policy-holes. Zaif can supply a much denser evidential substrate:\n\n```text\ntyped memories\n    ↓\nLibrarian comparison with existing patterns\n    ├── attach as an instance\n    ├── challenge or refine an existing pattern\n    ├── retain as a reference only\n    └── mint a candidate pattern\n                 ↓\n         pattern-conditioned recall\n                 ↓\n         cited use in a later task\n                 ↓\n         independently witnessed outcome\n                 ↓\n       promote / revise / merge / prune\n```\n\nThat four-way Librarian decision is crucial. Memory accumulation must not turn automatically into pattern proliferation.\n\nA revealing issue in zai-3’s notes\n\nZai-3 maps three a94A06 memories to `math-formalization/tactic-algebra-interference`. But the actual pattern is specifically about `rw`, `simp_rw`, and `convert` interfering with `Tendsto` or binder structure.\n\nThe `field_simp` memory is related only at a much broader level. There is an existing `field-simp-reciprocal` pattern, but that covers proving denominators nonzero—not the observed problem where the hypothesis and denominator are mathematically equal but syntactically differently normalized.\n\nTherefore the honest classification may be:\n\n- `tactic-algebra-interference`: a nearby pattern, but not a clean instantiation.\n- `field-simp-reciprocal`: another near-match, still incomplete.\n- The repeated lesson “normalize the denominator into the hypothesis’s syntactic form before `field_simp`” may justify a new candidate such as `math-formalization/normalize-before-field-simp`.\n\nThat is almost a perfect R17‴ worked example: memories reveal that nearest-neighbour attachment would conceal a meaningful structural distinction.\n\nOther paper examples\n\nA short examples box could include:\n\n- `structure/two-projections-of-one-quantity`: positive precedent. It was cited before it existed, the missing pattern was caught, then it was minted and later discharged its originating hole.\n- `process-coherence/status-refresh-before-work`: learned from the recurring failure of agents and selectors acting on stale mission banners.\n- `process-coherence/is-this-even-a-problem`: learned after 674 expensive ticks worked questions whose answers were already present in primary documents.\n- `normalize-before-field-simp`: prospective Zaif-derived candidate, grounded in typed proof episodes.\n- `polyrith unavailable`: negative example. This is a volatile environment fact, not a reusable pattern; retain it as reference memory.\n\nThese illustrate why new patterns are useful: they add a previously missing action to the repertoire. The two process-coherence patterns make “read and re-derive current reality first” eligible as the first box in future cascades. A field-simplification pattern would make a previously private Lean workaround retrievable across proofs.\n\nOne architectural adjustment to zai-3’s proposal follows from this. The system should not simply attach every memory to the best-scoring existing pattern. It needs an explicit `no-adequate-pattern` result. Otherwise retrieval similarity will absorb every novel episode into the nearest old category, and R17‴ will never fire.\n\nI would also model memory–pattern attachment as its own provenance-bearing, revisable claim rather than silently mutating the original `:memory/assert` edge. That lets the Librarian say who proposed the classification, with what confidence, against which rejected alternatives—and later revise it without rewriting the memory episode.\n\nI agree: R17‴ is the natural place, and Zaif exposes exactly what it should contain.\n\nOne correction first: after tracing the older material, I did find a partially live authoring route:\n\n`cascade library-gap → authoring → authored seed → pattern library`\n\nThe later slush specification expresses it as:\n\n`policy-hole → candidate-pattern/open → uniform prior → witnessed use`\n\nSo the War Machine can ingest new patterns, but the route is sparse, partly manual, and never became a coherent catalogue pattern. That is what R17‴ should repair.\n\nThe three supplements would then have a clean division:\n\n- R17′ — keep unresolved structural hypotheses explorable. Posterior spread is an honest uncertainty bonus, not EIG.\n- R17″ — generate possible reductions from embedding nearness. “These existing concepts might be mergeable.”\n- R17‴ — generate expansions from evidence-bearing holes. “The existing vocabulary cannot adequately describe this recurring situation.”\n\nA draft pattern would be:\n\n> Pattern Genesis from Evidence-Bearing Holes (R17‴).  \n> If independently recorded episodes, failed retrievals, or policy-holes repeatedly e